      "writtenOn": "2024-10-08T14:17:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We create a pipeline layout with an `internalImmediateDataSize` of 0 here every time a new PipelineLayout is created which seems useful to pre-initialize the cache.  Every `(Render|Compute)Pipeline::InitializeImpl` also initializes the layout with an `internalImmediateDataSize` of `kClampFragDepthArgsSize`. I think this would result in a minimum of 2 `VkPipelineLayout`s being created every time.\n\nYou could add a `constexpr size_t kDefaultInternalImmediateDataSize \u003d kClampFragDepthArgsSize + ...`. You can also assert that when the user push constant size is 0, the default matches the size that `*Pipeline::InitializeImpl` uses:\n\n```\n    // TODO(crbug.com/366291600): Add internal immediate data size when needed.\n    constexpr uint32_t userImmediateDataSize \u003d 0;\n    constexpr uint32_t internalImmediateDataSize \u003d kClampFragDepthArgsSize;\n    DAWN_ASSERT(internalImmediateDataSize \u003d\u003d kDefaultInternalImmediateDataSize);\n    DAWN_TRY(InitializeBase(layout, internalImmediateDataSize + userImmediateDataSize));\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 114,
        "startChar": 61,
        "endLine": 114,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "ef17bb99ec64a35957ac52926f923a0fbca4f2bf",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
